### TestBindingCommandsDocumentThemselves
$ stackmon inventory set-project --help
--- stdout ---
Bind an enrolled stack to the Docker Compose project its containers run in.

Without a binding, stackmon matches the stack to a project using the working
directory and compose file Docker recorded on that project's containers, and
reports an unknown identity rather than a guess when several projects match.

Pass --clear to drop the binding and go back to that automatic matching. The
stack's name, compose path, and enrollment date are left untouched.

Usage:
  stackmon inventory set-project <stack> <project> [flags]

Flags:
      --clear   remove the binding instead of setting one
  -h, --help    help for set-project

Global Flags:
      --config string      path to config.toml (default ~/.config/stackmon/config.toml)
      --inventory string   path to inventory.json (default ~/.local/state/stackmon/inventory.json)
--- exit 0 ---

### TestBindingCommandsDocumentThemselves
$ stackmon enroll --help
--- stdout ---
Add a stack to the inventory

Usage:
  stackmon enroll [<path>] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for enroll
      --name string      override the stack name (default: directory basename)
      --project string   bind the stack to this Docker Compose project (default: matched from the paths Docker recorded)
      --running string   enroll a running Compose project by project name

Global Flags:
      --config string      path to config.toml (default ~/.config/stackmon/config.toml)
      --inventory string   path to inventory.json (default ~/.local/state/stackmon/inventory.json)
--- exit 0 ---

